WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.082
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:02.082 --> 00:00:03.540
DANA BOEBINGER:
I'm Dana Boebinger,

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.690
a neuroscientist at the
McGovern Institute, at MIT.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.610
I study perception,
or how the brain

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.490
uses the senses to understand
the world around us.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.410
When your senses are
activated, your brain

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.900
is sent clues about what's
out there in the world.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.300
Usually, your senses
give you lots of clues,

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.310
and your brain pieces
these clues together

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.200
to figure out the
complete picture.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.412
But sometimes, the
clues aren't so clear,

00:00:24.412 --> 00:00:26.370
and your brain has to
make a guess about what's

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.800
out there based on your brain's
assumptions or expectations.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.130
So if you change
your expectations,

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.390
you can actually
change your perception.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:35.478
Here's what I mean.

00:00:35.478 --> 00:00:37.020
I'm going to play
a sound, and I want

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.440
you to listen for this word.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.300
You probably heard brainstorm.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.192
Now, I'm going to play
the exact same sound,

00:00:44.192 --> 00:00:45.900
but I want you to
listen for these words.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:51.280
You probably heard the words
green needle this time.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.940
That's because the audio quality
of this clip isn't clear,

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.320
and your brain
made an assumption

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.090
based on the clues it was given.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.640
You can visit our website to
experience other illusions

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.570
and learn more about perception.

